silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_6#gluediagramtoprightwhitespace a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline.sections.05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow.concrete_anchor_6#gluediagramtoprightwhitespace" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_concrete_anchor_6#gluediagramtoprightwhitespace silm:hasLongDescription "The GlueDiagramTopRightWhitespace is The empty top-right cell of the glue diagram is intentional layout: it preserves the visual gap that lets the three TypedLeg arrows fan into Mittens without label collisions, and lets the competing-cocone-target arrow Mittens -> VetCarePlan77 read cleanly as the unique mediating u. For the Mittens fixture (cat with vet record 77, microchip 2018, body mass 4.1kg), the empty cell records that VetCarePlan77 is a separate object that COULD be a competing apex, not a duplicate Mittens. Removing this whitespace would crowd the universal-property statement into the apex column and obscure the canonical-apex claim." .
